  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "quiet-room",
  "name": "Quiet Room",
  "tagline": "A close, quiet room: a soft, even grid and a warm chord. Almost no ambience.",
  "description": "A close, quiet room: only a faint warm room tone. A soft, round four-four close to you; even, soft sixteenth ticks; one deep note on the one and the three; a warm chord breathing underneath; a short chord now and then. Dry and narrow.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Detail",
    "for": "Precise work: code, figures, proofreading, checking.",
    "why": "The one variation that leaves the ambience out on purpose. For most people any noise bed slightly hurts careful work (it helps only those with attention difficulties), and the research keeps quiet as a real option. What is left is close, dry and narrow: an even grid of soft ticks for a steady frame, one bass note, a warm chord, no melody, nothing to pull your eye away."
  },
